# D1, one line per (degree, k). Columns: n = prime power nearest e^{u_k}; u-logn = u_k - log n; mu = KKT weight;
# 2L/sqn = 2 Lambda(n)/sqrt(n); g'' = gt''(u_k); W = W(h_k); kkt = W(h_k) - lambda h_k(0) - mu_k; h0 = h_k(0);
# eta0 = lambda/W(h_k); eta1/eta0 (inf: B_h < 0 on R); for eta = 2 eta0 (x2) and 10 eta0 (x10): R = trap radius around log n,
# lb/mu = weight lower bound / mu_k, extra = number of extra components of S found on the grid, rhomax = max eta h/gt on
# the grid away from the main component, rho_j = max_j eta h''(u_j)/gt''(u_j) over the other nodes, logs[m] = log m in S;
# verdict: isolates = S one interval containing no log m (m != n); single-but-wide = one interval containing another log m.
